urs {45,230,475,698,925,1680} are disjoint from 1860's in-neighbours {153,182,406,464,618,829,958,1390,1887}, so any influence path needs 3+ hops. The only connectivity between them runs through super-hubs (45, 67, 70, 274, 153, 156), which are the graph's top-activity nodes and account for 45's 412 triangles versus 3 and 13 for the endpoints. That is popularity-driven static reachability, not evidence of a chain whose consecutive events are each within 600 time units. With so few endpoint events in [18031, 56431], a 600-unit-tight multi-hop chain is not supported."}, "raw_final_response": "## Analysis\n\n**Endpoint sparsity (step_02).** Both endpoints are very low-activity: 1006 has 9 events / 9 distinct partners, 1860 has 11 events / 11 partners, against a graph of 16,325 events over a 100,000-unit horizon. So the *terminal* edge into 1860 has at most ~11 chances to land inside a 600-unit relay window, and 1006 has at most 9 emission opportunities in the queried interval [18031, 56431] \u2014 a slice covering ~38% of the horizon.\n\n**No short structural path (step_03, step_04).** 1006's out-neighbourhood {45, 230, 475, 698, 925, 1680} is *disjoint* from 1860's in-neighbourhood {153, 182, 406, 464, 618, 829, 958, 1390, 1887}. There is no 2-hop relay; any candidate cascade needs \u22653 hops, each of which must fire within 600 units of its predecessor.\n\n**The connection that does exist is a hub artefact (step_05, step_06, step_07, step_08).** The 2-hop neighbourhoods of both nodes are dominated by the same super-hubs (45, 67, 70, 14, 274, 153, 156, 904 \u2014 the top-activity list in step_07). Node 45 alone sits in 412 triangles versus 3 for 1006 and 13 for 1860 (step_08). So the time-ignoring \"connection\" between 1006 and 1860 is explained entirely by traffic through globally popular relays, which is precisely the confounder the task warns about: hub co-membership creates static reachability without implying any 600-unit-tight temporal chain.\n\n**Verdict.** The static path exists only via hubs, requires \u22653 hops, and the two endpoints are far too sparse for their handful of events to be chained under the strict 600-unit relay constraint. The evidence does not show a time-respecting cascade; it shows hub-mediated static connectivity.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_30df0d06\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1006, 1860],\n  \"window\": [18031, 56431],\n  \"confidence\": 0.62,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"1006 (9 events) and 1860 (11 events) are both extremely sparse and share no common relay: 1006's out-neighbours {45,230,475,698,925,1680} are disjoint from 1860's in-neighbours {153,182,406,464,618,829,958,1390,1887}, so any influence path needs 3+ hops. The only connectivity between them runs through super-hubs (45, 67, 70, 274, 153, 156), which are the graph's top-activity nodes and account for 45's 412 triangles versus 3 and 13 for the endpoints. That is popularity-driven static reachability, not evidence of a chain whose consecutive events are each within 600 time units. With so few endpoint events in [18031, 56431], a 600-unit-tight multi-hop chain is not supported.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 21264, "total_output_tokens": 3876, "total_tokens": 25140, "total_latency_ms": 56619, "llm_calls": 5, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}